# MANAGEMENT — backups, restores, recovery snapshots.
# Several requests here OVERWRITE data. Check the environment before each one.
# Demo-mode capture and restore → 08-demo-mode.rest.
# Rebuilding search (formerly "backfill-search") → 07-workflow.rest, C1.
# See README.md for environments and labels.

@snapshotId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000


# ═══ STATUS ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### READ ONLY — Most recent management job
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/management/status
Accept: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}

### READ ONLY — Recovery status
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/management/recovery/status
Accept: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}


# ═══ BACKUP (safe: only writes backup files) ═══════════════════════════════

### START — Back up the database to JSON files
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/management/backup
Accept: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}

### START — Take a recovery snapshot (copy its ID into @snapshotId)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/management/recovery/snapshots
Accept: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}


# ═══ RESTORE (overwrites the live database) ════════════════════════════════

### READ ONLY — Check whether a snapshot can be restored
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/management/recovery/restore/{{snapshotId}}/preflight
Accept: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}

### DESTRUCTIVE — Restore a snapshot over the live database
# Run preflight first. 409 "busy": wait for Retry-After and check status.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/management/recovery/restore/{{snapshotId}}
Accept: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}

### START — Resume an interrupted recovery
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/management/recovery/resume
Accept: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}

### DESTRUCTIVE — Seed: reload the database from the JSON backup files
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/management/seed
Accept: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}

### DESTRUCTIVE — Disaster recovery: rebuild from the original recipe files
# Scans the original photo folders and rebuilds placeholder family members.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/management/disaster-recovery
Accept: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}
